/*
 * audit.h — Security Audit & Security Event Logging Foundation (Step 21).
 *
 * Establishes a structured, tamper-aware, security-focused audit system
 * capable of recording security events generated by Steps 01-20.
 *
 * Architecture:
 *   SECURITY COMPONENT
 *          |
 *          v
 *   AUDIT SERVICE  <-- this layer
 *          |
 *          v
 *   EVENT VALIDATION
 *          |
 *          v
 *   AUDIT RECORD (ring buffer / storage)
 *          |
 *          v
 *   SECURE STORAGE
 *
 * The audit system OBSERVES and RECORDS security operations.
 * It does NOT decide whether an operation is allowed.
 *
 * Step 21 scope:
 *   - Structured security event model
 *   - Event type enumeration (identity, auth, password, attempt, MFA,
 *     session, authorization, RBAC, permission, security/system)
 *   - Event severity model
 *   - Event outcome model
 *   - Event validation (secret rejection, field validation)
 *   - In-memory ring buffer persistence
 *   - Storage abstraction interface
 *   - Controlled audit query with limits
 *   - Audit policy (severity thresholds, retention, required events)
 *   - Secret-safe auditing (password, key, token, biometric rejection)
 *   - Resource limits (max event size, metadata size, query limits)
 *   - Append-only security model
 *   - Integration points for all security subsystems
 *   - Concurrency-safe event recording
 *
 * NOT in scope:
 *   - GUI audit dashboard
 *   - SIEM integration
 *   - Remote centralized logging
 *   - Cloud audit service
 *   - Blockchain / hash-chain integrity
 *   - Security analytics / ML
 *   - Automatic incident response
 *   - External identity providers
 *   - Forensic platform
 */

